put":105,"cacheRead":14080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15521,"cost":{"input":0.00334,"output":0.001575,"cacheRead":0.0035199999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008435}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775767287729}}
{"type":"message","id":"2e42c89d","parentId":"5d142941","timestamp":"2026-04-09T20:41:31.676Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dEIwyMa3d6Xeqf5qLDTzDxnt|fc_011bc84ae0158e4f0169d80efab4c0819199f7e311c9b62137","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: slm-expert-backup\ndescription: Query a backup small language model (SLM) endpoint with expertise in nephrology, hypertension, and cardiology by asking a focused question grounded in retrieved records or clearly established conversation context, then processing the answer in the calling agent. Use when the agent needs a compact specialty model pass for kidney, blood-pressure, or cardiovascular interpretation, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded support, and does not need any adapter-loading step before inference.\n---\n\n# SLM Expert Backup\n\nUse this skill to ask the backup specialty SLM a focused question about nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context, then process the answer in the calling agent.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the task is within scope.\n   - Use this skill for nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology interpretation, summarization, pattern spotting, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded specialty questions.\n   - Prefer this skill when the user’s question concerns kidney disease, CKD, AKI, proteinuria, electrolytes, blood-pressure management, hypertensive organ damage, cardiovascular disease, cardiac risk, or cardiology follow-up.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build a focused question for the SLM.\n   - Write a single clear specialty question.\n   - Ground the question in retrieved records or clearly stated conversation facts.\n   - Keep it concise and specific.\n   - Do not invent findings, diagnoses, timelines, or test results.\n   - Good examples:\n     - `Based on this kidney-history summary, which findings most strongly support CKD progression and what follow-up should be prioritized?`\n     - `From this hypertension history, which missing details would matter most before judging whether control is adequate?`\n     - `Given these cardiovascular risk factors and symptoms, what cardiology-focused concerns deserve the closest follow-up?`\n     - `What nephrology and hypertension features best explain worsening renal function in this blood-pressure context?`\n\n3. Choose the specialty domain routing.\n   - Always send one or more domains with the question.\n   - Use only these values: `nephrology`, `hypertension`, `cardiology`.\n   - Choose the narrowest correct set.\n   - Use multiple domains only when the question genuinely spans them.\n   - Example mappings:\n     - CKD, AKI, proteinuria, renal imaging, electrolyte or acid-base questions -> `nephrology`\n     - Blood pressure control, resistant hypertension, antihypertensive strategy, hypertensive organ damage -> `hypertension`\n     - Cardiac symptoms, heart failure, ischemic risk, lipid or cardiovascular-risk questions -> `cardiology`\n     - Hypertensive kidney damage -> `nephrology`, `hypertension`\n     - Cardiorenal questions -> `nephrology`, `cardiology`\n\n4. Query the backup SLM without loading any adapter.\n   - Do not perform any adapter-load step.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py \\\n  --question \"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\" \\\n  --domain nephrology \\\n  --domain hypertension\n```\n\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"string\",\n  \"domains\": [\"string\"]\n}\n```\n\n   - Endpoint:\n\n```text\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\n```\n\n5. Read the response.\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\n\n6. Process the SLM answer in the calling agent.\n   - Do not treat the SLM output as the final user-facing answer by default.\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning, synthesis, or explanation.\n   - Cross-check it against the actual record or conversation context already available.\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\n   - If clinically relevant, highlight missing nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology history, red flags, or next-step questions.\n   - Treat the output as supportive specialty inference, not as a confirmed diagnosis.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn a response that includes:\n\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\n- **Domain(s)**: the domains used for the query\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775767291657}}
{"type":"message","id":"71f3ef80","parentId":"2e42c89d","timestamp":"2026-04-09T20:41:31.697Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CLWAu1rUdLH7wsaiG0KfkN1Z|fc_011bc84ae0158e4f0169d80efab4d08191bd056733bed572e0","toolName":"sessions_history","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:telegram:direct:495506013\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"✅ New session started · model: openai-codex/gpt-5.4\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openclaw\",\n      \"model\": \"delivery-mirror\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1775767238690\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"System: [2026-04-09 20:07:32 UTC] Exec completed (quick-ha, code 0) :: User: What are the symptoms of user latest symptoms? Assigner: Answer using TOEIC system: English version 2022 (version 7.0, release 1, interim report, July 2022). User: What are …\\n\\nA new session was started via /new or /reset. Run your Session Startup sequence - read the required files before responding to the user. Then greet the user in your configured persona, if one is provided. Be yourself - use your defined voice, mannerisms, and mood. Keep it to 1-3 sentences and ask what they want to do. If the runtime model differs from default_model in the system prompt, mention the default model. Do not mention internal steps, files, tools, or reasoning.\\nCurrent time: Thursday, April 9th, 2026 — 8:40 PM (UTC) / 2026-04-09 20:40 UTC\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1775767238735\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \" Hi — I’m ready to help